# The BAKED half of ~/.ssh/config inside ds-dev, copied into the image at
# /home/dev/ssh_config — one of gsrpi-dev-base's seams. At every start the base writes
#
#     /run/ds-secrets/ssh_config.fleet    (the host's ~/.ds-dev-secrets, read-only)
#     this file                           (the defaults, and nothing else)
#
# into ~/.ssh/config, in that order, because ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each
# keyword.
#
# It names NO IdentityFile and no github.com: GitHub is reached over https with the hub's
# token, never over ssh. Any identity this container should use for something else is that
# secrets directory's business — its id_* keys are copied into ~/.ssh, and its
# ssh_config.fleet names them.

# ── defaults — MUST stay last ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# ssh takes the FIRST value it obtains for each keyword, so a wildcard above a Host block
# silently wins over it. Anything specific belongs in ssh_config.fleet, which the base
# prepends above this.
Host *
  IdentitiesOnly yes
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 3
